@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Terms of Service";
}

<main class="policy-page">
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> October 29, 2026</p>

    <p>
        These terms apply to your use of AxertLMS, the Axert University learning
        management system. By using the service, you agree to follow these terms
        and applicable school policies.
    </p>

    <h2>Accounts and access</h2>
    <p>
        Use only an account assigned to you or created through an authorized
        registration process. Keep your sign-in credentials private and notify the
        service administrator if you believe your account has been accessed without
        permission. Access may depend on your role, registration status, and school
        approval.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>
        Use AxertLMS for its educational and administrative purposes. Do not attempt
        to disrupt, damage, or gain unauthorized access to the service, other
        accounts, or data. Do not use the service to upload or share unlawful,
        malicious, or unauthorized content.
    </p>

    <h2>Your information and connected services</h2>
    <p>
        Keep information you submit accurate and appropriate for the service.
        Google sign-in and Google Calendar are provided through Google and are also
        subject to Google's terms. Calendar access is optional and is requested when
        you choose to connect that feature.
    </p>

    <h2>Service availability and changes</h2>
    <p>
        Features may be updated, suspended, or unavailable for maintenance,
        security, or administrative reasons. The school may manage access in
        accordance with its policies.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
        For questions about these terms or the service, contact
        <a href="mailto:kurtcandrejo@gmail.com">kurtcandrejo@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>
</main>

<style>
    .policy-page {
        max-width: 900px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        line-height: 1.65;
    }

    .policy-page h1,
    .policy-page h2 {
        margin-top: 1.5rem;
    }

    .policy-page a {
        color: #8ab4f8;
    }
</style>
